DolphinXR changes to DolRecomp fa0cf619e8d7eb8cba7eaf55267a12caaebb46aa for Wii REL modules
(Mario Kart Wii's StaticR.rel), applied with: git -C <DolRecomp> apply <this file>

- 16-bit REL relocations (ADDR16, _LO, _HI, _HA) patch the halfword at the relocation's offset,
  as the SDK's OSLink does; they were written 2 bytes further, over the next instruction.
- --rel-bss <addr>: the BSS address a game gives a single REL (allocated apart from it).
- An executable section off the REL's alignment is a warning: the OS aligns the module only.
- Beside a REL's code: rel_layout.txt (header fields, section addresses) and rel_image.dol (the
  relocated code as a DOL at its address), which Tools/StaticRecomp/module-template consumes.

